\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Real actions and Gaussian states}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{Real fields acquire a topology, measurable events and a reference
volume before a [positive quadratic action](fdip-0004) defines a Gaussian probability.
The resulting [polynomial state](fdip-002X) has
[inverse precision as its covariance](fdip-000B).
[Kernel-orthogonal](fdip-000C) and [pinned constraints](fdip-0035) give two ways to obtain
massless laws, with different coordinate covariances.}
\p{The prerequisites below establish volume, spectral decomposition,
normalization and polynomial moments before the covariance theorem.
[Kernel separation](fdip-0033) gives exact massive normalizers and
[projected limits](fdip-0034); the [alternating four-cycle](fdip-0037)
evaluates the massive and massless formulas.}

